00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
MANUFACTURED LANDSCAPES is the striking new documentary on the
world and work of renowned artist Edward Burtynsky.

4
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Internationally acclaimed for his large-scale photographs of “manufactured landscapes”—quarries, recycling yards,
factories, mines and dams—Burtynsky creates stunningly beautiful art from civilization’s materials and debris.

5
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Self, played by Edward Burtynsky.

6
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Manufactured Landscapes is a 2006 Canadian documentary film about the
industrial landscape photography of Edward Burtynsky.

7
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
It was directed by Jennifer Baichwal and is distributed by Zeitgeist Films.

8
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It was the first of three documentary collaborations between Baichwall and Burtynsky,
followed by Watermark in 2013 and Anthropocene: The Human Epoch in 2018.

9
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film explores themes of factory, ship, pollution, china, shanghai, china.
